course: dictionary
lesson: 13497
title: Illustrate: pictures, examples and proof
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Illustrate is a verb. It has three main meanings. The first is to draw or add pictures to a book or story: «The artist will illustrate the new storybook.»
explain: The second meaning is to explain or show something using examples, diagrams or pictures: «The teacher drew a diagram to illustrate how the water cycle works.» Here the picture helps the idea become clear.
explain: The third meaning is to be an example that shows something is true: «Her quick answer illustrated that she really understood the sum.» Look at the clues around the word. Pictures usually mean the first meaning, and a diagram or example usually means the second or third.
fact: Illustrate means to draw pictures, to show something with examples or diagrams, or to be an example that proves something is true.
fact: An illustrated book is a book with pictures in it.
fact: «To illustrate the point» means to give an example that makes an idea clear.
fact: «This graph illustrates the rise in temperature.» means the graph shows that the temperature went up.
fact: Illustrate is a verb, so it changes: illustrates, illustrated and illustrating.
exercise: «The author asked Mia to illustrate her story about a dragon.» What does illustrate mean here? | To run fast to the end of the story | To delete the last page | *To draw pictures for the story | To read the story aloud
exercise: «Mr Patel used a diagram to illustrate how plants drink water.» What is the diagram for? | To hide the answer from the class | *To show how plants drink water | To decorate the classroom wall
exercise: «Her perfect test score illustrates that she has learned her times tables.» What does illustrates mean in this sentence? | To draw a picture of the test | To rub out a mistake | *To show that something is true | To copy a friend's work
test: «The book is beautifully illustrated, with a picture on every page.» What does illustrated mean? | Has been shortened | Has been read aloud in class | Has been printed in one colour only | *Has pictures added to it
test: «Use a clear example to illustrate your answer in science.» What is the best meaning here? | Hide your answer under a long story | Write your answer in capital letters | Copy the answer from the board | *Show your answer clearly with an example or picture
exam: Which sentence uses illustrate to mean "be an example that shows something is true"? | «The artist will illustrate the cover.» | «The children illustrated the stream on the map.» | «The teacher will illustrate the lesson on the board.» | *«Her kind deed illustrates how generous she is.»
